590	// ============================ native fp8 (e4m3) prefill path ============================
591	// QK and PV both run on the fp8 tensor core (2x bf16 throughput). The f32 accumulator layout for
592	// m64n128k32.e4m3 is identical to the bf16 m64n128k16 one, so softmax/mask/epilogue are unchanged.
593	// fp8 1-byte 128B swizzle: 128 fp8 = one 128B row; the 16-byte (16-fp8) chunk is swizzled by row&7.
594	// For hd128/CTA_N=128 every operand tile (Q,K,Vt,P) is a [128-row,128-col] K-major fp8 tile. The
595	// whole recipe (koff8 + LBO16/SBO1024/lt=1 + k32 step=kb*32 + V-transpose + P-in-smem SS-PV) is
596	// validated bit-exact vs a CPU fp8 GEMM in kernels/fp8_probe.cu.
597	// Row-count-generic fp8 128B swizzle: the col-block (c>=128) stride is 128*ROWS (# rows in the tile).
598	// ROWS=CTA_N reproduces the original koff8 exactly (and for HD<=128, c<128 so the col-block term is 0,
599	// making ROWS irrelevant -- byte-identical to the old koff8 on every existing hd128 path).
