    // the 128-lane COOP K/V gather latency (0.78-0.82x), whereas the high-occupancy per-tile grid hides
    // it ACROSS CTAs (0.85-0.89x). The dense GQA persist wins (1.02x) only because its K/V is TMA, not
    // COOP. Kept compiled (TMA_Q infra) for reference; per-tile+LPT is the paged-prefill path.
    if (paged && tmaq_ok && num_splits <= 1 && total_work >= 2L * num_sm_c && false) {
