// hd256: register-capped (acc_o[128] -> 1 CTA/SM, 18% occupancy), barrier/load-latency-bound. The
// CM=64 path (1 consumer WG) frees smem for a deeper STAGES=4 ring but loses the 2nd consumer
// warpgroup -> only 8 warps/SM (vs 12), measuring 0.72x: occupancy, not ring depth, is the binding
// constraint, and acc_o[128] hard-caps it at 1 CTA/SM. A head-dim-split (2 WGs on the same rows,
// each owning half of HDV at acc_o[64]) restores 12 warps + STAGES=4, but pays either a 1.5x
// redundant-QK cost or an asymmetric P-via-smem rewrite -- neither cleanly beats CM=128's 0.85x.
// Matching FA3's 0.92x at CN=80 needs CUTLASS's register allocator, which "no CUTLASS" forbids.
else if (hd == 256 && hdv == 256) PF_DISPATCH(256, 256, 3, 48, 128);

